but it may not hit the monster, and if you're close enough, it may hit
you. So the idea of "splashing" the monster is superfluous as it's
already handled both in the case of actually hitting it and (source
divers?) if I'm right by checking if it splashes it or in the negative
that it won't unless it's a direct hit. 


